{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
  "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State does not dispute that it waived the affirmative defense of limitations by failing to raise it in the District Court and by conceding in its answer that Day's petition was timely. Yet, nearly a year into the case, after the parties had briefed the merits, the magistrate judge not only raised an argument that the petition was untimely, he actually imposed the State's limitations defense and dismissed the case, despite the State's procedural default and contrary concession."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was a computation error. This is not a -- this is not a case where the State chose to waive the statute of limitations. It miscalculated. Isn't that the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, the -- it's right that there's an obligation if it notices it in the first instance on its first review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "does District Court have discretion to refer to the State for a response?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the better view of that clause is that it does not apply to an affirmative defense that's subject to waiver or tolling, that you can't say, based on an affirmative defense that's subject to waiver or tolling, that someone is plainly not entitled to relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And why shouldn't we treat this as a \"may\"? The judge noticed the clerical error and called it to the party's attention by an order to show cause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying that the error is simply that it wasn't done via Rule 15?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "derive -- and is directly addressed by Civil Rules 8 and 12. And this Court, in Gonzalez and Mayle, says that when that happens, that's where you start, with the civil rules."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0015",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "served by having the State calculate and make the motion, rather than putting the burden on the Federal Court to do it. The Court, we submit, should make the State -- they -- this Court, in Pliler, said the State's in the best position to make the limitations calculation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0016",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you want to make a motion to amend?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0017",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One that requires the court to raise it sua sponte, even if it's not raised by the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "shall not be granted unless you file within one year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Must there be good reasons for the judge to say, quote, \"I'm surprised that you haven't raised a statute of limitations defense\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BUSBY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For example, the Bendolph case that you have before you, there was an alteration in a date, and the Third Circuit didn't ascribe that to any particular person, but, nonetheless, the documents that the State had before it had the wrong date on it from which to calculate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, what's your answer as to whether there is any limitation on the judge just suggesting, \"By the way, you know, is there some reason why you haven't pleaded statute of limitations?\" Can a -- can a judge do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And what -- when would it be an abuse of discretion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BUSBY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judge's view was that the State had miscalculated under eleventh-amendment -- under Eleventh Circuit precedent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BUSBY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case has gone on down the road on another theory, and it's prejudicial to the parties, and it wastes -- it's a waste of the court's judicial resources to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We can dispose of it on that basis. And we can save all of those judicial and party resources by addressing that issue now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to begin by addressing the \"must\" versus \"may\" issue that Counsel discussed. For the reasons I mentioned, I think the better reading of the Eleventh Circuit's opinion is that there was an obligation, and that the most clear indication of that is its distinction of Esslinger, which expressly applied a Granberry-type analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1324",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-613083aad6ee-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Counsel. The case is submitted. [Whereupon, at 11:58 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
